WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.300
Supervised fine-tuning.

2
00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.167
This is the alignment step you will actually perform at work, and it needs nothing but good examples.

3
00:00:09.367 --> 00:00:10.933
Here's where SFT sits.

4
00:00:11.233 --> 00:00:13.100
First comes pretraining on the web.

5
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.833
Then SFT, where the model learns from demonstrations of the exact behaviour we want.

6
00:00:19.133 --> 00:00:23.433
And last, preference alignment with RLHF or DPO.

7
00:00:24.633 --> 00:00:28.433
SFT is plain supervised learning on demonstration data.

8
00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:33.092
Here is the prompt, here is the exact response the model should have produced.

9
00:00:33.092 --> 00:00:34.433
Minimize the difference.

10
00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:37.643
No preference rankings and no reward models.

11
00:00:37.643 --> 00:00:38.900
Just good examples.

12
00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:43.967
The lesson everyone learns the hard way: data quality dominates.

13
00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:50.233
A thousand excellent, hand checked demonstrations beat a hundred thousand scraped mediocre ones.

14
00:00:50.533 --> 00:00:55.099
The model imitates whatever you show it, including verbosity and mistakes.

15
00:00:55.099 --> 00:00:56.333
Curate, don't hoard.

16
00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:00.933
Here's SFT in code, using the TRL library.

17
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:05.467
We load a hundred hand checked conversations from a JSON lines file.

18
00:01:05.767 --> 00:01:09.957
Then we train a small Qwen model for three passes over the data.

19
00:01:09.957 --> 00:01:13.100
Afterwards, compare outputs on the same prompts.

20
00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:15.500
Picture this at work.

21
00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:20.400
You gather a hundred pairs: telemetry excerpt in, anomaly report out.

22
00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:23.967
A tiny model trains on them for three epochs, in minutes.

23
00:01:24.267 --> 00:01:29.067
Afterwards it writes severity, subsystem and impact without being asked.

24
00:01:29.067 --> 00:01:32.133
That before and after is how SFT becomes real.

25
00:01:33.333 --> 00:01:34.161
Let's recap.

26
00:01:34.161 --> 00:01:37.267
SFT is supervised learning on demonstrations.

27
00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:40.567
It comes after pretraining and before preference tuning.

28
00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.067
Data quality dominates everything.

29
00:01:43.367 --> 00:01:44.720
Curate, don't hoard.

30
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.667
Next up: LoRA.
